    <td style="padding-bottom: 4pt; font-size: 11pt; text-align: left"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></td><td style="padding-bottom: 4pt; font-size: 11pt; text-align: right"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></td><td style="padding-bottom: 4pt; font-size: 11pt; text-align: left"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>


</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 68 --><div>
    </div><div style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->60<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div><div>
    </div><div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div><div>
    </div><!-- Field: /Page --><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><b><i><span style="text-decoration:underline">Comparison
of Years Ended December 31, 2022 and 2021</span></i></b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><i>Revenue.</i></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">For the year ended December 31, 2022, our revenue
was $34,477,948, a decrease of $675,242, or 1.9%, compared to $35,153,190 for the year ended December 31, 2021. We operate our major business
in Thailand, where schools, bars and massage parlours have been closed, and alcohol sales have been banned in restaurants in a bid to
curb the pandemic until mid 2022. The continuous spread of COVID-19 in 2022 led to the decrease in our revenue in 2022. The frequency
of services delivered for our CIT and ATM management services business was affected as certain customers&#8217; facilities were closed
to curtail the spread of the coronavirus and the length of closures was longer as compared to the fiscal year 2021. Although there was
a drop in revenue for CIT related business, CP All Public Company, the largest business retailer in Thailand, became one of our top four
customers. We benefited from an increase and stronger demand for our GDM products and Robotics AI Solutions business by our customers.
For the year ended December 31, 2022, the revenue contribution from our Guardforce Digital Machine, or GDM product has experienced continuous
increase in the past years and it increased by $126,769 or 7.7%, which represents approximately 5.2% of our total revenue as compared
to 4.7% for the year ended December 31, 2021. For the year ended December 31, 2022, the revenue contribution from our Robotics AI Solutions
increased by $903,577 or 245.1%, which represents approximately 3.7% of our total revenue as compared to 1.0% for the year ended December
31, 2021. In addition, we acquired Handshake on March 25, 2021, which contributed $512,300 or 1.5% to our consolidated revenue for the
year ended December 31, 2022. In addition, we began operating in China in March 2022 by acquiring Shenzhen GFAI and Guangzhou GFAI, two
subsidiaries operating in robotics business and in June by acquiring Beijing Wanjia, a subsidiary operating in general security solutions
business. China has become our second largest geographic operation. However, our robotics business in China has been significantly impacted
by the Chinese government&#8217;s &#8220;Zero-Covid&#8221; policy until the fourth quarter of 2022 when the Chinese government lifted
such policy. Revenue contributed by Shenzhen GFAI and Guangzhou GFAI to our consolidated revenue for the year ended December 31, 2022
was $661,839. Revenue contributed by Beijing Wanjia to our consolidated revenue for the year ended December 31, 2022 was $1,785,789.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><i>Cost
of sales and gross profit.</i></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Cost
of sales:</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Cost&#160;of
sales consists primarily of internal labor cost and related benefits, and other overhead costs that are directly attributable to services
provided.&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">For the year ended December 31, 2022, our cost
of sales was $30,246,724, a decrease of $838,109, or 2.7%, compared to $31,084,833 for the year ended December 31, 2021. Cost of sales
as a percentage of our revenues decreased slightly from 88.4% for the year ended December 31, 2021, to 87.7% for the year ended December
31, 2022. This decrease was in line with the decrease in revenue. Despite fuel price, labor cost and other overhead costs continue to
rise due to inflation, we continue our effective cost controls and savings measures to control our direct labor and overhead cost.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Gross
profit:</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">As a percentage of revenue, our gross profit slightly
increased from 11.6% for the year ended December 31, 2021 to 12.3% for the year ended December 31, 2022 primarily due to cost controls.&#160;</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><i>Provision
for obsolete inventory</i>.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">During the year ended December 31, 2022, we made
a provision for our robots&#8217; inventory amounting to $942,882. This provision represents an estimate of the amount of inventory that
may not be sold at its original cost due to obsolescence, damage, or a decline in market value. Our inventory provision is determined
based on an analysis of historical sales trends, current market conditions, existing sales pipeline, and the age and condition of our
inventory. During the fiscal year 2022, we experienced a decrease in demand for our robots compared to our budget due to the impact from
COVID-19, resulting in excess inventory levels. This led to the recognition of a provision for inventory was needed as we adjusted our
estimates for potential losses on slow-moving or obsolete inventory.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">We have implemented measures to improve our inventory
forecasting and management, including the use of our GFAI ICP which provides advanced analytics and planning. Going forward, we will continue
monitoring our inventory levels and adjust our inventory provision as necessary. We believe that our proactive approach to inventory management
will enable us to maintain a healthy balance between inventory levels and sales performance, while mitigating the impact of losses on
our financial results. Overall, we believe that our inventory provision reflects our commitment to responsible inventory management and
our focus on delivering long-term value to our shareholders.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 69 --><div>
    </div><div style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->61<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div><div>
    </div><div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div><div>
    </div><!-- Field: /Page --><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><i>Impairment
loss on fixed assets</i>.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">During the year ended December 31, 2022, we recognized
an impairment loss of $4,408,037 on our robots&#8217; fixed assets. This impairment loss was primarily driven by our free trial business
model that shows an inadequate estimated future cash flow associated with these assets. This impairment loss reflects the reduction in
the value of the impaired assets and negatively impacts our financial performance.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="text-align: justify; margin: 0pt 0; font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Despite
this impairment loss, we remain committed to investing in our robots&#8217; assets to support our growth and expansion plans. We continue
to evaluate our fixed assets on a regular basis to ensure that they remain relevant and meet our operational needs. Going forward, we
will continue monitoring our fixed assets for indications of potential impairment and will adjust our estimates as necessary. We are
committed to investing in our assets in a prudent and responsible manner, while balancing the need for growth and innovation with the
need to maintain a strong balance sheet. Overall, we believe that our recognition of the impairment loss reflects our commitment to transparent
and responsible financial reporting, and our focus on delivering long-term value to our shareholders.&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><i>Selling,
distribution and administrative expenses.</i></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">The Company&#8217;s total selling, distribution
and administrative expenses are comprised primarily of selling expenses and administrative expenses.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%">
  <tr style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; vertical-align: top">
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></td>
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#9679;</span></td>
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Selling
    and distribution expenses are comprised of compensation and benefits for our sales and marketing personnel, travel and entertainment
    expenses, exhibitions, advertising and marketing promotion expenses, depreciation of motor vehicles, rental expenses, utility expenses
    and transportation charges.</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%">
  <tr style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; vertical-align: top">
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></td>
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 0.25in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">&#9679;</span></td>
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Administrative
    expenses are comprised of compensation and related expenses for our management and administrative personnel, depreciation of leasehold
    improvements and motor vehicles and rental expenses of our offices in different countries.</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">For
the year ended December 31, 2022, our total selling, distribution and administrative expenses were $15,320,201, an increase of $7,738,158,
or 102.1%, compared to $7,582,043 for the year ended December 31, 2021. The net increase was mainly due to:</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%">
  <tr style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; vertical-align: top">
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 24px"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></td>
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 24px"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">a)</span></td>
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Increase
    in headquarter expenses, including staff expenses, directors&#8217; emoluments, sales and marketing and for general corporate purposes
    and legal and professional fees in connection with the private placements, warrants solicitation, and acquisition of subsidiaries;
    and</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 100%">
  <tr style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; vertical-align: top">
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 24px"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></td>
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; width: 24px"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">b)</span></td>
    <td style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif; font-size: 10pt">Increase
    in robotics business expenses including staff expenses, rental expenses and marketing expenses to further our robotics as a service
    business and related technology capabilities. During the year ended December 31, 2022, we acquired four robotics related subsidiaries
    and incorporated twelve robotics related entities around the globe.</span></td></tr>
  </table><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Although we continue our cost reduction measures,
we expect our selling and distribution expenses will increase over time as we continue to expand our business and promote our Guardforce
brand. Our administrative expenses are expected to increase, reflecting the hiring of additional personnel and other costs related to
the anticipated growth of our business, as well as the higher costs of operating as a public company.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><i>Other
income</i>.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Other
income is comprised mainly of miscellaneous income, interest income and gain (loss) from disposal of fixed assets.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">For the year ended December 31, 2022, other income
was $88,732, a decrease of $196,489 or 68.9%, as compared to $285,220 for the year ended December 31, 2021. The decrease was mainly due
to a related party payable of $224,766 which was forgiven in May 2021, no such event incurred during the year ended December 31, 2022.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><i>Finance
costs.</i></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">Finance costs are comprised of finance charges
for leases, interest expense on interest-bearing bank borrowings, third party borrowing and related party borrowings utilized for working
capital purposes.</p><div>
</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">For
the year ended December 31, 2022, finance costs were $1,143,478, an increase of $158,635 or 16.1%, as compared to $984,843 for the year
ended December 31, 2021. The increase was due to the cash placement agent fee of $207,000 and accrued interest expense $22,767 in connection
with the convertible note we entered on October 25, 2022.&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><b>&#160;</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"></p><div>

</div><!-- Field: Page; Sequence: 70 --><div>
    </div><div style="margin-top: 12pt; margin-bottom: 6pt; border-bottom: Black 1.5pt solid"><p style="text-align: center; margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt"><!-- Field: Sequence; Type: Arabic; Name: PageNo -->62<!-- Field: /Sequence --></p></div><div>
    </div><div style="break-before: page; margin-top: 6pt; margin-bottom: 12pt"><p style="margin: 0pt">&#160;</p></div><div>
    </div><!-- Field: /Page --><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify">&#160;</p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><i>Income
tax (expense) benefit</i>.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">For
the year ended December 31, 2022, our income tax expense was $132,208, a decrease of $865,076, or 118.0%, as compared to income tax benefit
of $732,868 for the year ended December 31, 2021. During the year ended December 31, 2021, income tax benefit represents the recognition
of deferred taxes relating to the reported taxable loss in 2021 to be carried forward to offset future taxable profit as we believe it
is probable that taxable profits will be available against which the deferred tax asset can be utilized by fiscal year 2026. During December
31, 2022, we adjusted the overstated deferred tax asset to income tax expense in 2022 based on the estimate of our taxable profit available
to utilize against the deferred tax asset in the next five years.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">We
are subject to various rates of income tax under different jurisdictions. The following summarizes major factors affecting our applicable
tax rates in different countries we operate our business.</span></p><div>



</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><b>&#160;</b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><b><i>Cayman
Islands</i></b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">We
are incorporated in the Cayman Islands. Under the current laws of the Cayman Islands, we are not subject to income, corporation or capital
gains tax in the Cayman Islands.&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif"><b><i>British
Virgin Islands</i></b></span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Our
subsidiary incorporated in the BVI is not subject to taxation in the British Virgin Islands.</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">Our
operating subsidiaries incorporated in different tax jurisdiction are subject to different corporate income tax rate as follows:</span></p><div>

</div><p style="font: 10pt Times New Roman, Times, Serif; margin: 0pt 0 0pt 0.5in; text-align: justify"><span style="font-family: Times New Roman, Times, Serif">&#160;</span></p><div>

